  "key_insight": "CPU big-core temperature crossed the same ~67 C envelope on BOTH throttling runs (wave-4 vanilla iter6 @ 67.1 C and wave-8 v1_fa2_selective iter10 @ 77.9 C) while DDR sat 5-10 C lower at the same instant. The non-throttling watchdog run (wave-9 v1_fa2_stack) held CPU big-core <= 66.8 C the whole time. CPU big-core temp may be the better single predictor of throttle than DDR alone."
